From 1fb16ad619233c9c92390d4666ecbaf69363f103 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 19:37:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Accept collapsed digit runs in AIRIO and radio numeric
 commands

Speech engines apply inverse text normalisation to spoken digit runs, so
"five eight eight" reaches VoiceAttack as "588" rather than "5 8 8". The
laser code, datalink tune, TACAN tune and radio frequency handlers read one
digit per {CMDSEGMENT:n}, which assumes the opposite. When the run collapses
the command either fails to match or, if a concatenated phrase is used, the
whole number lands in the first segment and the rest silently parse as zero
(e.g. "laser code 688" was sent as 68800).

Read the digits with {TXTNUM:"{CMD}"} instead, which returns them in order
regardless of how the engine segmented them. This is the approach the F-4E
WSO handlers already use in WSOCommandHandler.GetNumberFromCommand().

Existing profiles that emit one digit per segment produce identical results.

Also replaces the silent zero-fill with a length check, so an unreadable
command reports rather than actioning a wrong value, and accepts the full
four-digit laser code since the leading 1 is fixed in hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
